          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            The best wet basement solution is <strong class="text-white">whichever one matches your actual symptom, tried in order from cheapest to most invasive</strong>. Fix gutters, downspouts, and grading first — it's free and solves more than you'd expect. Seal damp walls with a coating, inject specific cracks, and reserve an interior drain and sump pump for basements that genuinely flood. Save exterior excavation for the rare case that actually needs it, and never let a contractor sell you Tier 5 for a Tier 1 problem.
